      "id": "claim_f57056aa606545a78db7d0274987474f",
      "statement": "Service configuration is declaratively defined in two setup files: ulabase.setup.ts (base configuration that imports environment.ts and derives the server's registration/verification/password-reset/invitations/oauth flags from the app's feature flags; its steps install the accounts feature with 409 \"already installed\" tolerated, set the branding name, sync the accounts feature config, optionally add Google OAuth credentials, add the app origin to origin-allowlist without replacing existing origins, and end with an exported appPointsAtService step that rewrites only the apiUrl line of environment.ts) and ulabase.setup.consents.ts (reuses those accounts steps and adds the consents gate in six steps: a userConsentsSchema, its attachment to the /users collection via the /users _meta jsonSchema.schemaId, a userCanPatchOwnConsents permission that stamps TOS_VERSION/PP_VERSION and @now server-side, the two latestConsents account-properties-claims, a guards feature install, and a consentsGate rule answering 451 with on_error allow). Both are documented in the Service Setup page.",
